From 167c49a3bd3c55b5a2326da4ae2745f27a2b744f Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Keith Packard <keithp@keithp.com>
Date: Sat, 21 Nov 2026 05:29:09 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 16/20] test-posix: Check the configuration part of <unistd.h>

The version and option macros take values POSIX allows, every _SC_,
_PC_ and _CS_ name is defined with a distinct value, sysconf and
confstr accept them all, the getopt variables and remaining functions
have POSIX's types, and in strict mode crypt, encrypt, gethostid, swab,
getpagesize, getpass and optreset stay hidden.
---
 test/test-posix/test-unistd/CMakeLists.txt    |   1 +
 test/test-posix/test-unistd/meson.build       |   1 +
 .../test-unistd/test-unistd_h-config.c        | 808 ++++++++++++++++++
 .../test-unistd/test-unistd_h-names.c         |  14 +
 4 files changed, 824 insertions(+)
 create mode 100644 test/test-posix/test-unistd/test-unistd_h-config.c

